MMPS governing rule

The performer stations prepare the performers. The console runs the show.

Console responsibilities

The console is the single source of truth for:

performance selection
shared show clock
choreography timeline
music control
all stage-wide lighting
Stage Halo
drum and speaker lighting cues
stage effects
start, pause, resume, stop, and emergency stop
readiness and diagnostics
Performer station responsibilities

Each local station handles only its own performer:

performer login or seat detection
role assignment
instrument selection
prop rez, attach, replace, and detach
local animation library
local readiness state
reporting status to the console


MMPS Governing Rule #2

Every MMPS device must identify itself using the standard MMPS Device Identity Protocol.

That means:

Future devices work automatically.
Builder Mode becomes universal.
Device Manager never needs to know device-specific code.
Discovery becomes automatic.
Diagnostics become automatic.
Firmware updates become automatic later.


MMPS Governing Rule #3

Every configuration change made by a user must be available through the Console.
If we ever find ourselves saying:
"Just edit the script..."
We've broken the rule.
